1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,310
Split the interest finer and finer —
does the money grow forever?

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:07,080
Put 1 into an imaginary bank
that pays 100% interest a year

3
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:09,050
After a year, one payment of interest: 1 → 2

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,020
What if it pays 50% twice, every half year?

5
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:13,590
1.5, then another 50% → 2.25
The interest earns interest too!

6
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:18,960
Let's split it even finer

7
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:22,730
The finer we split, the more we get…
but each gain gets smaller

8
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:26,000
Even split into every second, every instant,
it never passes 2.718…

9
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:29,370
That limit is the number e:
where (1 + 1/n) multiplied n times ends up

10
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:32,870
Anything that grows or shrinks nonstop —
e always shows up in the math

11
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:37,620
NEXT: Measuring angles with length?
Radians
